WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.152
Let’s bring the main ideas together.

00:00:02.152 --> 00:00:06.112
Def creates a function. Parentheses call it.

00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:12.737
Parameters make inputs flexible. Return sends reusable results back to the program.

00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:18.830
Docstrings explain purpose, and small functions can be combined into larger workflows.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:25.667
Next, we move into lists and tuples so functions can work with structured collections of values.

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:31.255
In Module 4, we’ll give those functions more structured data to work with.

00:00:31.255 --> 00:00:38.320
You’ll learn how lists and tuples store collections of values, how to access and update those values,

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.861
and how to process an entire collection rather than working with one value at a time.
